From: Galeria contributors
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: SDR parent surfaces with independently HDR media

App-scoped backport for GTK 4.22. GDK_MEDIA_ONLY_HDR=1 keeps parent/popup
surfaces SDR, while graphics-offload subsurfaces retain their media color
state. HDR memory textures use compositor-advertised RGBA16F shared buffers
rather than the debug path's SDR 8-bit Cairo conversion. No public ABI change.
GTK source license: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/gdk/wayland/gdksurface-wayland.c
+++ b/gdk/wayland/gdksurface-wayland.c
@@ -892,6 +892,10 @@
                      "preferred color state, surface %p color state %s",
                      self, gdk_color_state_get_name (color_state));
 
+  /* Keep SDR UI on the parent; offloaded media has its own color state. */
+  if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("GDK_MEDIA_ONLY_HDR"), "1") == 0)
+    color_state = gdk_color_state_get_srgb ();
+
   gdk_surface_set_color_state (GDK_SURFACE (self), color_state);
 
   self->color_state_changed = TRUE;
